1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:06,711
When the gods and the demons churned the ocean of milk, the first thing it gave up was poison.

2
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:10,498
Halahala: dark enough to end every world.

3
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:17,220
Shiva took it in his hands, and drank it. He held it in his throat, and his throat turned blue.

4
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:25,322
So he is called Neelakantha, the blue-throated one: the destroyer who saved the world from destruction.

5
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:40,022
He is the ascetic of Mount Kailash, the first of all yogis, and the dancer whose steps undo the world, so that it can begin again.

6
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:51,093
In the south of India, five great temples honour him as the five elements of which everything is made.

7
00:00:57,317 --> 00:01:04,709
Earth, at Kanchipuram, where he is worshipped in a lingam of sand, beneath an ancient mango tree.

8
00:01:12,317 --> 00:01:20,059
Water, at Thiruvanaikaval, where a spring rises in the sanctum, and the shrine is never fully dry.

9
00:01:27,317 --> 00:01:36,021
Fire, at Tiruvannamalai. Each year, at the festival of Karthigai, a great flame is lit on the summit of the hill.

10
00:01:42,317 --> 00:01:49,701
Air, at Srikalahasti, where a lamp in the inner shrine is said to flicker, though no wind can reach it.

11
00:01:57,317 --> 00:02:01,925
And space, at Chidambaram, where he dances as Nataraja.

12
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:12,092
Behind a curtain there, the secret of Chidambaram is revealed: an empty space. Nothing to see, because the formless has no form.

13
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:19,746
His mantra has five syllables, one for each element.

14
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:27,717
Na. Ma. Shi. Va. Ya.

15
00:02:31,517 --> 00:02:33,780
Om Namah Shivaya.

16
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:50,262
The world is painted, kept, and washed away. And the paper beneath it was always there.
